widget.solution:
def count_trades(trades):
    counts = {}
    for t in trades:
        counts[t] = counts.get(t, 0) + 1
    return counts

explain.text:
`get` with a default of 0 covers a ticker's first appearance, so one line does the counting. An `if t in counts:` branch would also work, at twice the length.

